1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,540
Well, thank you all so much again for joining us. We just wrapped up a series on solitude, and next week we are launching a series on the Book of Ruth, which I am very, very excited about. But what I am probably as excited about, if not more excited about, is our guest speaker this morning. We are welcoming a friend that is connected to us through the denomination.

2
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:51,080
I'm calling her a new friend of mine. She came out to lead our women in their conference yesterday. We had seven churches with 65 women here yesterday, which is awesome. Sarah is a published author and mother and cool person, so please give her a warm canvas welcome.

3
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:28,120
Am I on? Am I on? Okay. Good morning, everybody. Cool person. I don't know if I can agree with that, but I'm going to go with it, so thank you. I am also, I work from home, and I don't normally wear dress shoes, so I'm going to say this is holy ground and take off my shoes because my toes are starting to go numb, and I just, I guess my feet don't fit in those shoes anymore.

4
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:44,120
So, I am really delighted to be here with you and worshiping with you this morning. It was just wonderful. I feel so blessed. I always weep during worship, so I was like, "Oh, gosh. This is going to be bad." But thank you.

5
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:58,160
I have the distinct honor of standing before you today in what I call prime real estate on the church calendar. Right between Ash Wednesday, when we're reminded that we are dust and

6
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:10,160
just shall return and the start of Lent, when many people in the family of God commemorate Christ's 40 days in the wilderness by making the ultimate sacrifice, giving up chocolate.

7
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:27,700
Here we are, caught between our own mortality and voluntary suffering. What a comforting place to be right now. There's nothing like a little existential dread and self-denial to really set the tone for the season.

8
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:38,700
In this perfect storm of dust and deprivation, I want to point out the face in the eye of this hurricane. Anxiety.

9
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:56,860
Maybe you recognize this character from Pixar's Inside Out 2. This is Anxiety. She is the queen of over-preparation and over-analysis. When she's allowed to reign over our fear and our suffering,

10
00:02:57,240 --> 00:03:06,240
she can create quite the storm of self-doubt and panic attacks. But let's be honest, life gives us plenty to be anxious about.

11
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:16,240
We worry about our families, our jobs, our health, the state of the world. Some of us are even anxious about what we should give up for Lent.

12
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:26,240
While anxiety is a normal human emotion and something we all experience in different ways, sometimes she can turn into a beast.

13
00:03:26,780 --> 00:03:41,780
God and His goodness has given us His Word, His Spirit, His community, and His creation as ways to help us fight against the spirit of fear and anxiety that threatens to take us down.

14
00:03:41,780 --> 00:03:56,320
Today, as we stand in this tension between the reminder of our limits and the call to rely on God, I want to explore what it means to face our anxiety with faith.

15
00:03:56,320 --> 00:04:03,320
To bring our fears into God's presence, and to trust that we are held, even when life feels uncertain.

16
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:11,320
When I feel anxious about practically anything, it helps me to remember this reality:

17
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:25,860
For I am convinced that neither death nor life, neither angels nor demons, neither the present nor the future, nor any powers, neither height nor depth,

18
00:04:25,860 --> 00:04:33,860
anything else in all creation, will be able to separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord.

19
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:44,860
Romans 8:38-39. It's easy for us to plow through that set of verses and feel lightly inspired. I got a few amens, I heard.

20
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:50,860
So I'd like to read it again to you, slower and even more dramatically this time.

21
00:04:50,860 --> 00:05:01,860
For I am convinced that neither death nor life, neither angels nor demons, neither the present nor the future, nor any powers,

22
00:05:01,860 --> 00:05:12,860
neither height nor depth, nor anything else in all creation, will be able to separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord.

23
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:19,860
Nothing in creation can separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord.

24
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:28,860
I don't think that you're feeling the full weight of this passage yet, so we're just going to keep on saying it over and over for the next 30 minutes.

25
00:05:28,860 --> 00:05:36,860
Let's start with neither death nor life. This little bit is especially pertinent on the heels of Ash Wednesday.

26
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:48,860
Nothing can separate us from God's love in Jesus Christ, not living and not dying. Saint Benedict and other monks of old incorporated the

27
00:05:48,860 --> 00:05:57,860
phrase "memento mori" into their spiritual practice. Memento mori means remember that you must die.

28
00:05:57,860 --> 00:06:06,860
I realize this might seem counterintuitive to the whole anxiety-reducing objective of this sermon, but stick with me.

29
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:17,860
When I remember that none of us gets out of here alive, it has a way of right-sizing my problems. Practically nothing I am worried about today has eternal consequences.

30
00:06:17,860 --> 00:06:28,860
And nothing I am worried about can separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord, not even dying.

31
00:06:28,860 --> 00:06:46,860
Okay, neither angels nor demons. As much as C.S. Lewis' demons in the screw-tape letters or the spiritual forces depicted in John Milton's Paradise Lost might try, even the supernatural world that we don't understand

32
00:06:46,860 --> 00:07:00,860
but love to imagine, can't get between us and God's love. Neither good spirits nor evil spirits, they can't stand against the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord.

33
00:07:00,860 --> 00:07:10,860
How about the present or the future? What present and future challenges feel like barriers to accessing God's love?

34
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:15,860
Perhaps you are afraid you're going to miss God's plan for you.

35
00:07:15,860 --> 00:07:22,860
Perhaps you are afraid of losing your job. Perhaps you are afraid you'll be found out for who you really are.

36
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:29,860
Perhaps you are afraid your child will not choose to be the person you envision them becoming.

37
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:36,860
Perhaps you are afraid of where the world is headed. Perhaps you are afraid you aren't a good enough Christian.

38
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:42,860
Perhaps you are afraid you will never measure up to earn your place in God's kingdom.

39
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:54,860
Brothers and sisters in Christ, let me join my voice with Paul, who says, "The Spirit you received does not make you slaves, so that you live in fear again.

40
00:07:54,860 --> 00:08:03,860
Rather, the Spirit you received brought about your adoption to sonship, and by him we cry, "Abba, Father."

41
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:10,860
Nothing in the present or the future is beyond the loving embrace of "Abba, Father."

42
00:08:10,860 --> 00:08:24,860
Well, what about those powers? There are lots of powers and principalities in the world, both foreign and domestic, that are conjuring up all kinds of anxieties today.

43
00:08:24,860 --> 00:08:32,860
Of all of the things to be worried about, it would seem that this is a concern we ought to be worried about.

44
00:08:32,860 --> 00:08:51,860
After all, in Ephesians, Paul reminds us that our struggle isn't against flesh and blood, but against the rulers, against the authorities, against the powers of this dark world, and against the spiritual forces of evil in the heavenly realms.

45
00:08:51,860 --> 00:08:59,860
Interesting enough, Paul doesn't urge us to take up weapons of war to go to battle against the powers.

46
00:08:59,860 --> 00:09:07,860
If that was what Jesus expected us to do, he might have set up a different example for us the night that he was betrayed.

47
00:09:07,860 --> 00:09:14,860
He had every opportunity, and even a band of brothers, ready to pick up arms on his behalf.

48
00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:26,860
Peter even made a go at it, but Jesus told him, "Put your sword back in its place, for all who draw the sword will die by the sword."

49
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:32,860
To help us understand how we ought to face the powers and principalities of this dark world,

50
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:39,860
Paul invites us to wear the belt of truth, don the breastplate of righteousness,

51
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:46,860
fit our feet with the gospel of peace, and hold in front of us the shield of faith.

52
00:09:46,860 --> 00:09:54,860
And what is the shield of faith? Our belief that there is nothing that can separate us from the love of God

53
00:09:54,860 --> 00:10:00,860
that is in Christ Jesus, our Lord. These words from Paul should empower us

54
00:10:00,860 --> 00:10:06,860
to stand firm in our conviction to follow Christ, who is the way, the truth, and the life,

55
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:14,860
wielding the sword of truth, which is the word of God, as we face individual and systemic injustices,

56
00:10:14,860 --> 00:10:22,860
defend the poor, feed the hungry, care for the widows and orphans, heal the sick, and shelter the outsider.

57
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:30,860
All right, let's scoot along into the final leg of this verse. Neither height nor depth,

58
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:40,860
nor anything else in all creation. In all of creation, Christ and the love of God that is in Christ Jesus, our Lord.

59
00:10:40,860 --> 00:10:45,860
I got real good at memorizing this verse when I was working on this sermon, by the way.

60
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:50,860
In all of creation, Christ reigns supreme.

61
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:56,860
In Colossians 1, verses 15 through 20, Paul tells the church of Colossae,

62
00:10:56,860 --> 00:11:03,860
"The sun is the image of the invisible God, the firstborn over all creation.

63
00:11:03,860 --> 00:11:11,860
For in him all things were created, things in heaven and on earth, visible and invisible,

64
00:11:11,860 --> 00:11:18,860
whether thrones or powers or rulers or authorities. All things have been created through him and for him.

65
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:24,860
He is before all things, and in him all things hold together.

66
00:11:24,860 --> 00:11:31,860
And he is the head of the body, the church. He is the beginning and the firstborn from among the dead,

67
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:39,860
so that in everything he might have the supremacy. For God was pleased to have all his fullness dwell in him,

68
00:11:39,860 --> 00:11:46,860
and through him to reconcile to himself all things, whether things on earth or things in heaven,

69
00:11:46,860 --> 00:11:51,860
by making peace through his blood shed on the cross.

70
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:57,860
I love how many times Paul says all things in this passage of Scripture,

71
00:11:57,860 --> 00:12:05,860
as if to really hit home how supreme Christ is. He's the firstborn over all creation.

72
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:14,860
In him all things were created. All things have been created through him and for him. He is before all things.

73
00:12:14,860 --> 00:12:20,860
In him all things hold together. Is there anything outside of all things?

74
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:28,860
No, there's nothing outside of all things. Way back in the second century AD,

75
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:36,860
Irenaeus, who is one of the early church fathers, developed what we call today the two-books theology.

76
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:42,860
According to Irenaeus, God has written for us two books. I bet you didn't know that.

77
00:12:42,860 --> 00:12:48,860
A big book of creation, and a little book, the Bible.

78
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:56,860
And that is through, that it is through both of these so-called books, that God has chosen to reveal his character.

79
00:12:56,860 --> 00:13:00,860
I love this because I love being out in nature.

80
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:06,860
A little side note, we had a really lovely time hiking in Shenandoah before coming here this week.

81
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:10,860
It's just glorious. So your backyard is very beautiful.

82
00:13:10,860 --> 00:13:18,860
We have the incredible privilege to live during a time of substantial scientific advancement.

83
00:13:18,860 --> 00:13:23,860
We can see far greater heights than we've ever seen before.

84
00:13:23,860 --> 00:13:32,860
Scientists now estimate that there are somewhere between 200 billion to 2 trillion galaxies in the known universe.

85
00:13:32,860 --> 00:13:38,860
All creation is far higher and wider than we can even imagine.

86
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:48,860
At the same time, we can also zoom in to the greatest depths to examine the very framework of all of creation.

87
00:13:48,860 --> 00:13:56,860
In my lifetime, we were once pretty sure that the atom was the building block, the smallest particle in creation.

88
00:13:56,860 --> 00:14:00,860
Then we discovered that there were more bits and pieces to the atom,

89
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:05,860
and then we learned that there were even smaller bits and pieces inside those bits and pieces.

90
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:11,860
All creation is far deeper and complex than we can even imagine.

91
00:14:11,860 --> 00:14:18,860
And yet, science is once again confirming what the wisdom teachers have been declaring for centuries.

92
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:20,860
All things are interconnected.

93
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:30,860
"We are stardust brought to life, then empowered by the universe to figure itself out," says agnostic scientist Neil deGrasse Tyson.

94
00:14:30,860 --> 00:14:37,860
"But we know the one who empowers the universe. It is in Christ that all things hold together."

95
00:14:37,860 --> 00:14:44,860
I said at the beginning that this is a sermon on anxiety, sandwiched between death and suffering.

96
00:14:44,860 --> 00:14:55,860
We've peered into creation to see how high and wide and long and deep the love of God is that is in Christ Jesus our Lord.

97
00:14:55,860 --> 00:15:07,860
If God's love is that high and that wide and that long and that deep, and we can't be separated from it, that should give us so much confidence.

98
00:15:07,860 --> 00:15:14,860
In the grand scheme of things, nothing can separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord.

99
00:15:14,860 --> 00:15:21,860
But God is not just a God of the universal. God is also a God of the particular.

100
00:15:21,860 --> 00:15:28,860
And we can't talk about anxiety without talking about the birds and the flowers.

101
00:15:28,860 --> 00:15:33,860
As part of Jesus's most famous sermon, he told his followers,

102
00:15:33,860 --> 00:15:42,860
"Therefore I tell you, do not worry about your life, what you will eat or drink, or about your body, what you will wear.

103
00:15:42,860 --> 00:15:47,860
Is not life more than food, and the body more than clothes?

104
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:56,860
Look at the birds of the air. They do not sow or reap or store away in barns, and yet your heavenly Father feeds them.

105
00:15:56,860 --> 00:16:05,860
Are you not much more valuable than they? Can any one of you be worrying by worrying at a single hour to your life?

106
00:16:05,860 --> 00:16:13,860
And why do you worry about clothes? See how the flowers of the field grow? They do not labor or spin.

107
00:16:13,860 --> 00:16:19,860
Yet I tell you that not even Solomon, in all his splendor, was dressed like one of these.

108
00:16:19,860 --> 00:16:31,860
If that is how God clothes the grass of the field, which is here today and tomorrow is thrown into the fire, will he not much more clothe you, you of little faith?

109
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:38,860
So do not worry, saying, "What shall we eat?" or "What shall we drink?" or "What shall we wear?"

110
00:16:38,860 --> 00:16:44,860
For the pagans run after all of these things, and your heavenly Father knows that you need them.

111
00:16:44,860 --> 00:16:51,860
But seek first his kingdom and his righteousness, and all these things will be given to you as well.

112
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:57,860
Therefore, do not worry about tomorrow, for tomorrow will worry about itself.

113
00:16:57,860 --> 00:17:06,860
Each day has enough trouble of its own. God does not only care about the grand plan of his coming kingdom.

114
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:19,860
God doesn't just hold all of eternity in the palms of his hands. God also sees you. He loves you. He cares for you.

115
00:17:19,860 --> 00:17:25,860
Everything, even you, are held in the immensity of God's love.

116
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:33,860
The psalmist sings of this intimate reality, this way God knows you personally, in Psalm 139.

117
00:17:33,860 --> 00:17:39,860
For you created my inmost being. You knit me together in my mother's womb.

118
00:17:39,860 --> 00:17:47,860
I praise you because I am fearfully and wonderfully made. Your works are wonderful. I know that full well.

119
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:55,860
My frame was not hidden from you when I was made in the secret place, when I was woven together in the depths of the earth.

120
00:17:55,860 --> 00:18:05,860
Your eyes saw my unformed body. All the days ordained for me were written in your book before one of them came to be.

121
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:15,860
All of this allows us to trust that God holds all things together, no matter what happens. No matter what.

122
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:23,860
We can spin out every kind of worst-case scenario and still land on this grand truth.

123
00:18:23,860 --> 00:18:29,860
Nothing can separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord.

124
00:18:29,860 --> 00:18:35,860
Our belief in the reality of God's love should revolutionize the way we live our lives.

125
00:18:35,860 --> 00:18:46,860
We are set free by this great love. Through Christ's love, we no longer conform to the patterns of this world, but are transformed by the renewing of our minds.

126
00:18:46,860 --> 00:18:51,860
Through Christ, we are given abundant life. We are empowered by the Holy Spirit

127
00:18:51,860 --> 00:19:05,860
to love the unlovable, called to reflect the image of God that is in every single human being, so they can see and believe that they too are loved with an everlasting love.

128
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:18,860
So that they too can be set free of the shackles of sin and death, and truly live by the grace of God, with peace that passes all understanding and joy that overflows.

129
00:19:18,860 --> 00:19:30,860
Empowered by the confidence of God's great love, every single person we meet, from the moment we wake up to the second we put our heads on our pillows, is a person we can extend God's love to.

130
00:19:30,860 --> 00:19:45,860
Not looking past the unlovable, or the strange, or the outsider, but instead seeing the image of God in them. Treating them as children of God. Loving them as Christ loves us.

131
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:54,860
This kind of foundation reframes every interaction we have with other human beings, even our enemies.

132
00:19:54,860 --> 00:20:09,860
God has already done the work. God has already said that we are redeemed, once and for all, through the work of Christ on the cross, so that nothing can separate us from the love of God.

133
00:20:09,860 --> 00:20:25,860
But we just don't always believe it. I just don't always believe it. It is easy for me to forget that nothing can separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus, our Lord.

134
00:20:25,860 --> 00:20:36,860
As I wait for blood work and test results, it is easy to forget that nothing can separate me from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus, my Lord.

135
00:20:36,860 --> 00:20:49,860
As my children trip and stumble through their own sequence of existential questions, it is easy for me to forget that nothing can separate them from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus, our Lord.

136
00:20:49,860 --> 00:21:01,860
As I scroll through social media and watch the unfolding apocalypse, it is easy to forget that nothing can separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus, our Lord.

137
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:14,860
So, I join my voice with the Father in Mark chapter 9, verse 24, who said to Jesus, "I do believe. Help me overcome my unbelief."

138
00:21:14,860 --> 00:21:28,860
You see, in my head, I believe that Christ Jesus is Lord. I believe He's the way, the truth, and the life. But sometimes, in my heart, I'm not so sure.

139
00:21:28,860 --> 00:21:40,860
My heart says, "That's nice, what you believe about God, brain. But are you sure He's got this? Even this? Are you sure?"

140
00:21:40,860 --> 00:21:52,860
Because maybe I need to take matters into my own hands and worry about this thing that is completely beyond my control. That seems really productive.

141
00:21:52,860 --> 00:22:01,860
The redemptive work of Christ is done, once and for all. But we still live in the reality of right now.

142
00:22:01,860 --> 00:22:08,860
And there will always be this part of us on this side of the grave that just isn't so sure He is faithful.

143
00:22:08,860 --> 00:22:16,860
His faithfulness never ceases. I believe it. So Lord, help me overcome my unbelief.

144
00:22:16,860 --> 00:22:26,860
Help me open up the vice grip of control I have of my life in my fists and trust that you are really the way, the truth, and the life.

145
00:22:26,860 --> 00:22:38,860
Help me walk in your ways so I can truly experience the indescribable, uncontainable love of the Father and peace Christ promised.

146
00:22:38,860 --> 00:22:47,860
The world is full of trouble. Jesus did not promise to rescue us from this sandwich of suffering and death.

147
00:22:47,860 --> 00:23:03,860
Instead, he said, "I have told you these things so that in me you may have peace. In this world you will have trouble, but take heart. I have overcome the world."

148
00:23:03,860 --> 00:23:16,860
Take heart, heart. Jesus has overcome the world. I cling to these promises from Jesus, and when my anxiety rises over that which is out of my control,

149
00:23:16,860 --> 00:23:26,860
I seek reminders in nature, in my community, in prayer, and in Scripture of the love that holds all things together.

150
00:23:26,860 --> 00:23:41,860
I join my shaky, anxious voice with 14th century church mystic Julian of Norwich, who said, "All shall be well. All shall be well. All manner of things shall be well."

151
00:23:41,860 --> 00:23:55,860
When anxiety rises up in your life, I pray that you, being rooted and established in that great love, may have power, together with all the Lord's holy people,

152
00:23:55,860 --> 00:24:12,860
to grasp how wide and long and high and deep is the love of Christ, and to know this love that passes under our knowledge, that you may be filled to the measure of all the fullness of God.

153
00:24:12,860 --> 00:24:24,860
May the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord be the foundation that gives us the ability to stand firm in times of fear and uncertainty,

154
00:24:24,860 --> 00:24:35,860
and continue to do the good work the Lord has called us to do. Amen. Will you join me in prayer?

155
00:24:35,860 --> 00:24:45,860
Oh, Father, thank you so much for being with us this morning. Thank you for your amazing presence that holds all things together,

156
00:24:45,860 --> 00:24:53,860
that holds me together, and catches all of my nerves into a little container and says, "Be confident."

157
00:24:53,860 --> 00:24:59,860
Lord, thank you that you hold our world together, that no matter what is happening,

158
00:24:59,860 --> 00:25:06,860
the powers and the principalities in our families and in our friend groups, in our church and in our communities,

159
00:25:06,860 --> 00:25:14,860
you hold all things together. Your love conquers all. I thank you so much for these people.

160
00:25:14,860 --> 00:25:22,860
I thank you for the opportunity to gather here this morning for your amazing word that reassures us that you have a love

161
00:25:22,860 --> 00:25:31,860
for us that is everlasting. I pray that you would be with us here today as we continue to lift our eyes and our hearts

162
00:25:31,860 --> 00:25:39,860
and our minds to you and be with us as we leave this precious day.

163
00:25:39,860 --> 00:25:49,860
Take my shoes and my water that I didn't drink and my paperclip.

164
00:25:51,860 --> 00:26:02,860
We're going to conclude our service by taking the bread and the cup of communion.

165
00:26:02,860 --> 00:26:14,860
I wanted to read a verse before we did so as we contemplate what we're doing when we come up and get this little cube of bread and this small cup of juice.

166
00:26:14,860 --> 00:26:20,860
It's so much more than what we often think about when we approach the table.

167
00:26:20,860 --> 00:26:40,860
We talked about at our Ash Wednesday service that I think that there's a way in which we can preach the gospel in the church in America that so emphasizes what God did on the cross, that it totally ignores any invitation for us to follow him to that same cross.

168
00:26:41,860 --> 00:26:57,860
And we even do that in communion. Oftentimes, I do that, and I think it's good to remember in communion that the body broken for us, the blood shed for us, is the finished work on the cross, that there is nothing that we can do to inherit our salvation.

169
00:26:57,860 --> 00:27:08,860
There is nothing we can do to earn our salvation. It is a free gift from God and from God alone. And yet, we read words from Jesus like this in Matthew chapter 16.

170
00:27:08,860 --> 00:27:19,860
Then Jesus said to his disciples, "Whoever wants to be my disciple must deny themselves, take up their cross, and follow me.

171
00:27:19,860 --> 00:27:25,860
For whoever wants to save their life will lose it, but whoever loses their life for me will find it.

172
00:27:25,860 --> 00:27:30,860
What good will it be for someone to gain the whole world and yet forfeit their soul?

173
00:27:30,860 --> 00:27:37,860
Or what can anyone give in exchange for their soul? For the Son of Man is going to come in the Father's glory with his angels,

174
00:27:37,860 --> 00:27:43,860
and then he will reward each person according to what they have done."

175
00:27:43,860 --> 00:27:50,860
And so at Canvas, we practice an open communion. That means you don't have to be a member of our church to take this.

176
00:27:50,860 --> 00:27:58,860
It's between you and the Lord, but communion is a thing that is set up by Jesus for his followers.

177
00:27:58,860 --> 00:28:06,860
And so this morning as we come to the table to partake in communion, I was thinking about the song we sang,

178
00:28:06,860 --> 00:28:18,860
at first, lead me to the cross. And that's often a song that when I sing it, I think about Jesus leading me to the cross to receive his forgiveness and his grace, his mercy and his love.

179
00:28:18,860 --> 00:28:24,860
But I think just like communion is a reminder for us to experience his grace, his mercy, his forgiveness, his love.

180
00:28:24,860 --> 00:28:35,860
It's also an invitation for us to follow Jesus's example, to lay down our life for those around us, to pick up our cross and to follow after him.

181
00:28:35,860 --> 00:28:49,860
And so this morning, as we take communion, I'd love for you to think about not only what God has done for you by going to the cross, but what he's invited you to follow him into.

182
00:28:49,860 --> 00:29:04,860
To follow his example of laying down our life, serving and loving others wholly imperfectly, which is again, the beauty of the reminder of God's forgiveness and grace at the table is you and I are going to fail 10 minutes after

183
00:29:04,860 --> 00:29:17,860
we leave this door. Some of us five minutes after we leave this door. Some of us before we get out of the room. But that does not negate the invitation that Jesus' mercies are new every morning.

184
00:29:17,860 --> 00:29:30,860
Every moment of every day, we have the opportunity to repent and to move forward in obedience to Jesus. And so I think we have a map on the screen. We do.

185
00:29:30,860 --> 00:29:39,860
I'm going to dismiss you for those of you who want to say, "I want to remind myself of God's grace and forgiveness through His broken body and shed blood."

186
00:29:39,860 --> 00:29:47,860
But not only that, I want to take seriously His invitation to follow His example. I'd invite you to come and grab the elements.

187
00:29:47,860 --> 00:29:55,720
And once you get them and get seated, we will take them together. So, go ahead.
